        "type": "Module",
        "name": "preamplifier",
        "description": "NE5532 dual op-amp used as a low-level preamplifier stage to provide the initial voltage gain (roughly 20-40x, configurable via external feedback network). Second channel unused. Single-ended audio input is applied to IN1_P (non-inverting input of channel 1). IN1_N (inverting input) receives feedback for gain setting. OUT1 provides amplified audio signal to feed the power amplifier. Uses VCC_P and VCC_N pins to split the 9V supply rail; external biasing network (mid-supply virtual ground reference) required for single-supply operation.",
        "id": "preamplifier"
